{"availability":"available","full":"PolThm/5-news","name":"5-news","description":"Five news stories a day, ranked by how many independent sources agree — deterministic filtering, no engagement optimisation, and a page that ends.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-10T13:32:34Z","updated":"2026-10-11T11:37:52Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://5-news.vercel.app","topics":["astro","bmad-method","claude","cohere","data-pipeline","gdelt","news-aggregator","pwa","python","static-site"],"demo":"https://5-news.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:57.422Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:57.422Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:57.422Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:50:57.422Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Five stories a day, chosen by how many independent sources agree — never by an editor, never by a model.","Most news products optimise for engagement. This one optimises for finishing: it shows at most five items, tells you exactly why each one is there, and then ends the page. No infinite scroll, no recommendations, no \"you might also like\".","The product is the filter, not the writing. A ranked list of five raw headlines with links is already useful; five AI summaries of arbitrarily chosen stories are worthless."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/PolThm/5-news/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3d7bd376432b0d73de43527312d18966e210a0e2d3c713ac565dab8d29bc3026","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:57.560Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:57.560Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Five stories a day, chosen by how many independent sources agree — never by an editor, never by a model.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/PolThm/5-news/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"3d7bd376432b0d73de43527312d18966e210a0e2d3c713ac565dab8d29bc3026","sour